# Feature 3: soft delete for comments

Rules relied on (read the values from the named source):
- policy-soft-delete.md: what delete does, which comments lists show, who may delete.
- policy-error-response.md: shape of new error responses; status codes stay the same.
- code-comment-model.md: current Comment fields. The deletion timestamp is new.
- code-comment-ownership.md: existing not-found handling in deleteComment. Keep the status code only.
- code-auth-header.md: how the request's user is identified (author check).
- code-migrations.md: schema file, migration folder, deploy command, database address variable.
- policy-release-checklist.md: fresh-database check and undo note for each migration.
- code-test-layout.md: where unit tests go and how to run them.

Scope:
- Add one nullable deletion timestamp to Comment in a new migration.
- deleteComment sets that timestamp and keeps the row. Only the author may delete.
- getCommentsByArticle leaves out comments that have the timestamp set.
- Error bodies for this feature follow policy-error-response.md.

Out of scope: editing (policy-edit-window.md, policy-edited-at-marker.md).
